WEBVTT

00:00:09.615 --> 00:00:14.245
Hatenkou Yugi

00:00:15.320 --> 00:00:18.556
The departure always comes unexpectedly

00:00:18.557 --> 00:00:22.027
It is destined to happen like a coincidence

00:00:22.027 --> 00:00:27.829
Your evolving fate starts to grind

00:00:28.901 --> 00:00:32.268
Confused by sudden rain

00:00:32.437 --> 00:00:35.706
Stunned by getting rejected and soaked in the rain

00:00:35.707 --> 00:00:41.805
Let’s laugh it off: a new path will open for you

00:00:42.447 --> 00:00:45.616
What’s the most precious thing

00:00:45.617 --> 00:00:49.187
That’s hidden behind meaningless things

00:00:49.187 --> 00:00:57.094
You can make miracles happen, so keep smiling

00:00:57.763 --> 00:01:00.596
My Heartbreaking Romance

00:01:00.799 --> 00:01:04.836
Let’s go wild as you desire

00:01:04.836 --> 00:01:10.138
Have a blast and live it up: that’s my style

00:01:11.043 --> 00:01:14.171
Your Heartrending Sorrow

00:01:14.479 --> 00:01:18.416
| will leave it alone for now

00:01:18.417 --> 00:01:24.879
So let’s begin our adventure right here

00:01:25.157 --> 00:01:29.992
Am | ever

00:01:32.431 --> 00:01:33.796
| can see the light.

00:01:34.800 --> 00:01:37.325
That’s the light of hope in life.

00:01:37.869 --> 00:01:44.104
This is the cave that my grandfather once took
me and my little sister to when we were kids.

00:01:44.676 --> 00:01:49.010
He told us he was keeping
something important hidden.

00:01:49.982 --> 00:01:51.813
Listen carefully.

00:01:52.284 --> 00:01:56.277
There’s something very important
that I’ve kept here.

00:01:57.389 --> 00:02:01.792
But now that I’m getting old,
| suppose | have no use for it.

00:02:02.127 --> 00:02:04.152
So I'd like you girls to have it.

00:02:04.563 --> 00:02:11.731
When you grow up, come back here whenever
you encounter a hardship or lose hope in life.

00:02:15.607 --> 00:02:19.703
| believe it will help you in some way.

00:02:20.946 --> 00:02:23.312
It has been one year
since my grandfather passed away.

00:02:24.850 --> 00:02:28.786
Now with the passage of time,
| can’t remember what it was.

00:02:29.888 --> 00:02:37.351
But | feel that what’s hidden deep in the cave
is calling out to me at times.

00:02:38.330 --> 00:02:40.161
Telling me that now is the time.

00:02:42.401 --> 00:02:47.930
And tonight, | see the light
as if it’s lighting up my life.

00:02:53.545 --> 00:02:57.140
Must Mot
Violate Paradise

00:02:57.883 --> 00:03:02.286
Jeez, | can’t believe | got lost in this downpour.

00:03:03.088 --> 00:03:07.286
Heat-tan might be captured by a wicked witch
in the forest and may be stewed in a cauldron.

00:03:08.460 --> 00:03:12.692
With no lantern, Alzeid might be falling from a cliff.

00:03:13.065 --> 00:03:15.192
They better snap out of it on their own.

00:03:16.968 --> 00:03:18.060
It’s chilly.

00:03:18.370 --> 00:03:20.930
If this goes on, I'll totally catch a cold.

00:03:22.541 --> 00:03:24.309
Huh? Oh, great.

00:03:24.309 --> 00:03:26.573
What am | supposed to do without a light?

00:03:32.317 --> 00:03:34.251
Looks like I’m saved.

00:03:47.199 --> 00:03:48.188
Good evening.

00:03:48.366 --> 00:03:51.699
I’m a poor, helpless girl who got lost in the rain.

00:03:52.170 --> 00:03:56.004
Would you let this wayfarer spend the night
sheltering from the rain?

00:03:57.709 --> 00:03:58.573
No.

00:03:59.778 --> 00:04:01.946
Could you possibly be more blunt than that?!

00:04:01.947 --> 00:04:04.415
C’mon, let me try one more time!

00:04:06.885 --> 00:04:08.079
You must be troubled.

00:04:08.620 --> 00:04:10.554
Please, come on in.

00:04:10.789 --> 00:04:13.952
Th-thank you very much.

00:04:15.460 --> 00:04:18.759
What’s the idea? | thought | turned her away.

00:04:19.197 --> 00:04:23.031
But Sister, she must be at a loss in this rain.

00:04:23.168 --> 00:04:24.795
We could at least provide the guest room.

00:04:25.637 --> 00:04:28.003
Of course not. How impudent.

00:04:28.406 --> 00:04:33.105
But remember what Father told us?
To be kind to people in need.

00:04:33.278 --> 00:04:34.438
Kind?

00:04:34.646 --> 00:04:36.204
What a hypocrite.

00:04:36.515 --> 00:04:40.110
You obviously don’t care much
for my opinion, anyway.

00:04:40.485 --> 00:04:42.544
If my approval is all you want, don’t bother.

00:04:46.124 --> 00:04:48.718
| apologize for my sister’s behavior.

00:04:50.729 --> 00:04:53.789
Please follow me.
The fireplace will warm you up.

00:04:54.032 --> 00:04:55.624
S-sure.

00:04:56.434 --> 00:05:00.734
By the way, | got separated
from my two travel companions,

00:05:01.006 --> 00:05:02.473
so if they show up here...

00:05:02.808 --> 00:05:05.641
Your companions? Well...

00:05:08.914 --> 00:05:09.778
Huh?!

00:05:09.981 --> 00:05:10.915
Hey!

00:05:10.916 --> 00:05:12.110
What took you so long?

00:05:12.284 --> 00:05:14.252
What are you guys doing here?

00:05:14.252 --> 00:05:17.380
Didn’t you get my telepathic message
telling you where we are?

00:05:17.923 --> 00:05:20.118
You’re on my reject list.

00:05:20.258 --> 00:05:22.852
| was losing my patience, and about to go to bed.

00:05:23.094 --> 00:05:24.662
I’m glad you found your companions.

00:05:24.663 --> 00:05:31.933
Well, we don’t have much to offer,
but please make yourselves comfortable.

00:05:32.103 --> 00:05:34.435
Not much to offer? That’s not true.

00:05:34.940 --> 00:05:37.135
What a beautiful lady you are.

00:05:38.977 --> 00:05:42.378
Sorry. He’s a bit off his rocker.

00:05:45.116 --> 00:05:46.310
Well, excuse me.

00:05:50.422 --> 00:05:51.389
Um...

00:05:51.890 --> 00:05:53.380
About my sister...

00:05:53.592 --> 00:05:55.890
Sure, leave it to us.

00:06:00.498 --> 00:06:03.558
What sheer bliss.

00:06:03.768 --> 00:06:05.702
That was a close call.

00:06:05.871 --> 00:06:08.704
My heartfelt thanks to that pretty lady.

00:06:09.074 --> 00:06:12.908
Let’s forget about what the other one said...

00:06:14.312 --> 00:06:15.313
I’m coming in.

00:06:15.313 --> 00:06:18.476
Oh, sure. Um... Miss?

00:06:18.783 --> 00:06:19.772
lt's Madeila.

00:06:20.151 --> 00:06:22.052
My sister asked me to bring you a towel.

00:06:22.053 --> 00:06:23.213
Thank you.

00:06:23.388 --> 00:06:28.985
Listen, if you aren’t traveling on urgent business,
| was wondering if you could help me.

00:06:29.527 --> 00:06:31.961
| wouldn’t mind offering a reward
for your work, of course.

00:06:32.197 --> 00:06:33.926
You wouldn’t mind, huh?

00:06:34.099 --> 00:06:38.559
I’d like to go to college,
but my parents are against it.

00:06:39.104 --> 00:06:41.538
| have no choice,
so I’m thinking about leaving home,

00:06:41.740 --> 00:06:42.968
but | don’t have enough money.

00:06:43.108 --> 00:06:45.542
Um, it’s totally over my head.

00:06:45.911 --> 00:06:48.513
Oh, c’mon. I’m just getting to the point now.

00:06:48.513 --> 00:06:54.474
My grandfather who passed away last year
kept a hidden treasure in the cave on our property.

00:06:54.753 --> 00:06:56.220
Oh, you want to steal it?

00:06:56.488 --> 00:06:58.547
It doesn’t necessarily mean stealing.

00:06:58.924 --> 00:07:02.027
He promised to give it to us once we grew up.

00:07:02.027 --> 00:07:03.128
But...

00:07:03.128 --> 00:07:06.231
Besides, don’t you owe me
for letting you stay here?

00:07:06.231 --> 00:07:08.032
You better be useful, at least.

00:07:08.033 --> 00:07:11.569
Well, your sister was kind.

00:07:11.569 --> 00:07:12.695
Shut up.

00:07:13.238 --> 00:07:14.671
Tomorrow, okay?

00:07:15.674 --> 00:07:17.107
What was that about?

00:07:17.542 --> 00:07:19.442
| guess she’s at a difficult age.

00:07:19.878 --> 00:07:20.970
So, now what?

00:07:21.413 --> 00:07:22.903
I’m not sure.

00:07:23.982 --> 00:07:27.485
By the way, you’re the type
who starts by shampooing, huh?

00:07:27.485 --> 00:07:28.417
Huh?

00:07:29.521 --> 00:07:30.579
Just you wait and see.

00:07:30.755 --> 00:07:34.748
ll do such an amazing job
that she’ll be sorry for assigning it to me.

00:07:48.106 --> 00:07:49.164
Wh-who’s there?!

00:07:49.341 --> 00:07:51.366
Come on, it’s time for treasure hunting.

00:07:51.509 --> 00:07:52.942
It’s still the middle of the night!

00:07:53.078 --> 00:07:54.579
The early bird catches the worm, right?

00:07:54.579 --> 00:07:56.638
Let’s find treasure!

00:07:57.349 --> 00:07:58.748
Oh, jeez...

00:07:58.917 --> 00:08:00.214
are you trying to annoy me?

00:08:00.385 --> 00:08:02.683
You're exactly right, Miss Client.

00:08:03.355 --> 00:08:07.815
"Treating someone that is discourteous
with even more discourtesy" is my family motto.

00:08:08.159 --> 00:08:10.423
I’m gonna make you cry. Brace yourself.

00:08:11.896 --> 00:08:13.261
It’s right beneath our feet.

00:08:14.366 --> 00:08:15.300
What do you think?

00:08:15.300 --> 00:08:16.665
Of course we'll go down.

00:08:17.635 --> 00:08:18.260
Go!

00:08:28.480 --> 00:08:31.381
Wow, that was a blast like a roller coaster!

00:08:31.750 --> 00:08:32.944
How could you?!

00:08:33.318 --> 00:08:35.183
Wow, this is it, huh?

00:08:35.854 --> 00:08:36.513
Hm’?

00:08:37.188 --> 00:08:40.646
“Enter at your own risk”?

00:08:41.359 --> 00:08:42.326
Very well.

00:08:42.494 --> 00:08:43.862
C’mon, let’s go.

00:08:43.862 --> 00:08:45.193
Woo-hoo!

00:08:45.597 --> 00:08:47.861
Let’s have a picnic lunch!

00:08:48.266 --> 00:08:49.893
Don’t forget some sugar cubes, too.

00:08:50.168 --> 00:08:51.658
What are you guys doing here?

00:08:51.903 --> 00:08:53.336
Wait, sugar cubes?

00:08:54.139 --> 00:08:55.936
Sugar is an essential nutrient, you know.

00:08:56.141 --> 00:08:58.336
Treasure hunting excites
a man’s spirit of adventure.

00:08:59.010 --> 00:09:00.568
Whatever.

00:09:01.346 --> 00:09:02.313
What is that?

00:09:03.114 --> 00:09:05.344
Whoa, how scary! It ticks me off!

00:09:05.517 --> 00:09:07.552
Your word choice for describing
your emotion is totally off.

00:09:07.552 --> 00:09:09.918
Don’t you find this exciting
just like an amusement park?

00:09:10.655 --> 00:09:11.781
For instance...

00:09:11.990 --> 00:09:12.649
Oh.

00:09:13.858 --> 00:09:15.223
Look what | found.

00:09:20.065 --> 00:09:20.759
Whoopsie.

00:09:26.604 --> 00:09:28.936
Wow, what a view!

00:09:29.841 --> 00:09:31.240
Alright, go ahead.

00:09:33.511 --> 00:09:35.445
Stop looking for trouble.

00:09:35.613 --> 00:09:36.739
Okay.

00:09:41.352 --> 00:09:42.376
Whoopsie.

00:09:46.391 --> 00:09:49.121
Aren’t you supposed to protect me?

00:09:49.294 --> 00:09:50.428
Oh, did you forget?

00:09:50.428 --> 00:09:53.556
It was your grandfather who set this trap.

00:09:54.099 --> 00:09:57.702
He went to all this trouble to protect it;
you better take his challenge seriously.

00:09:57.702 --> 00:09:59.470
Heels.
He went to all this trouble to protect it;
you better take his challenge seriously.

00:09:59.471 --> 00:10:00.870
A fight between the heels.

00:10:01.072 --> 00:10:02.440
Shall we go on ahead?

00:10:02.440 --> 00:10:03.304
Yeah.

00:10:04.876 --> 00:10:08.437
Why don’t you give in already
and ask for help?

00:10:09.447 --> 00:10:12.041
When it comes down to it,
| have only myself to rely on.

00:10:13.551 --> 00:10:16.748
If that’s what you believe,
shouldn’t you stop relying on others?

00:10:17.021 --> 00:10:19.285
You can handle everything on your own, right?

00:10:19.624 --> 00:10:21.319
If you wish, we can leave you alone right here...

00:10:22.560 --> 00:10:23.458
What’s wrong?

00:10:25.296 --> 00:10:29.255
When | was a child, | almost drowned once.

00:10:30.768 --> 00:10:36.707
My sister and | took a boat
out on the lake when no one was around.

00:10:37.575 --> 00:10:42.376
The boat capsized by accident,
and we were thrown into the lake.

00:10:43.882 --> 00:10:47.079
Our parents rushed to the scene
when they heard our screams.

00:10:48.086 --> 00:10:49.781
My sister was the only one that they rescued.

00:10:52.557 --> 00:10:54.218
Then | realized...

00:10:55.160 --> 00:10:57.185
they chose my sister.

00:10:58.396 --> 00:11:02.924
lt makes sense to save the one with low stamina.

00:11:03.201 --> 00:11:07.797
Unlike my sister, I’m neither
good-looking nor good-natured.

00:11:07.939 --> 00:11:10.772
Whichever they prefer isn’t the point.

00:11:11.009 --> 00:11:12.237
| don’t know about that.

00:11:12.577 --> 00:11:16.707
Isn’t it the perfect situation
to help you judge things more clearly?

00:11:17.215 --> 00:11:20.446
“What are the chances
of being able to save them both?”

00:11:21.419 --> 00:11:25.549
“If only one can be saved,
which one is more worthwhile?"

00:11:25.990 --> 00:11:28.458
“And, which is more precious?”

00:11:32.063 --> 00:11:34.899
Is that why you fear water and can’t move?

00:11:34.899 --> 00:11:36.230
That’s absurd.

00:11:36.434 --> 00:11:37.833
How would you find treasures like that?

00:11:38.069 --> 00:11:41.539
Tell me, if those two behind you
were drowning simultaneously,

00:11:41.539 --> 00:11:42.801
which would you choose?

00:11:53.351 --> 00:11:54.784
Never mind. I’m just kidding.

00:11:57.121 --> 00:11:58.455
Let’s keep going.

00:11:58.456 --> 00:11:59.650
Huh?!

00:12:18.343 --> 00:12:19.571
| can see the light.

00:12:21.079 --> 00:12:23.240
Isn’t that my grandfather's?

00:12:24.015 --> 00:12:24.913
But...

00:12:26.351 --> 00:12:28.342
What's the matter, Madeila?

00:12:29.320 --> 00:12:31.720
Isn’t it too soon to give up?

00:12:32.924 --> 00:12:36.087
My precious treasure is right in front of you.

00:12:37.662 --> 00:12:38.754
Is that...

00:12:41.833 --> 00:12:42.891
G’morning.

00:12:44.235 --> 00:12:46.203
Luckily, no one was hurt.

00:12:46.871 --> 00:12:47.769
The thing is...

00:12:48.539 --> 00:12:51.975
| searched around the area
but it doesn’t look like there’s a way out.

00:12:52.343 --> 00:12:58.612
Either way, your grandfather
picked an awful place to hide the treasure.

00:13:00.084 --> 00:13:03.417
Just to be sure,
Heat-tan and Alzeid are searching again.

00:13:03.688 --> 00:13:05.713
But | guess it’s just a waste of time.

00:13:10.895 --> 00:13:13.764
We're trapped here,
and yet you act like nothing’s wrong.

00:13:13.765 --> 00:13:16.632
Or do you have a solution in mind?

00:13:19.103 --> 00:13:23.267
Not really. With our magic and stuff,
we can easily get out.

00:13:23.608 --> 00:13:24.909
| mean, the three of us.

00:13:24.909 --> 00:13:26.843
What do you mean, the three of you?

00:13:27.178 --> 00:13:28.479
Wait a second.

00:13:28.479 --> 00:13:30.140
What about me?

00:13:30.615 --> 00:13:33.117
We'll abandon you, Miss Client.

00:13:33.117 --> 00:13:35.745
After all, | don’t really like you.

00:13:36.354 --> 00:13:39.323
There’s no way I'll put myself
in danger for you.

00:13:39.757 --> 00:13:44.319
I’m not gonna risk my life
for someone who’s not even my friend.

00:13:46.264 --> 00:13:50.928
You're right. At the end of the day,
even my own parents abandoned me!

00:13:51.402 --> 00:13:53.131
Someone like me doesn’t deserve to liv—

00:13:54.706 --> 00:13:56.606
Wh-what’s the idea?!

00:13:56.908 --> 00:13:58.705
You’re way too depressing!

00:13:58.943 --> 00:14:01.478
Put forth effort to brighten your life, at least.

00:14:01.479 --> 00:14:04.448
Wait, that’s a slipper from our bathroom.

00:14:04.449 --> 00:14:06.617
| guess it followed me
so that | could slap you with it.

00:14:06.617 --> 00:14:07.311
How touching.

00:14:07.585 --> 00:14:09.019
Like the slipper can talk!

00:14:09.020 --> 00:14:11.956
Girls have lots of energy, huh?
“Man, | wanna slap her,
punch her, and beat her up.”

00:14:11.956 --> 00:14:13.924
Should | make them be quiet?
"| want to see you weep."

00:14:13.925 --> 00:14:16.655
Cut it out! My slippers would never talk like that!

00:14:16.961 --> 00:14:20.522
Not only are you ugly both inside and out,
but also extremely paranoid.

00:14:20.898 --> 00:14:22.833
You totally disgust me.

00:14:22.834 --> 00:14:24.235
You’re going too far!

00:14:24.235 --> 00:14:28.572
Then, is that all you’re worth?

00:14:28.573 --> 00:14:29.972
What are your strong points?

00:14:30.408 --> 00:14:31.739
What are the things you are proud of?

00:14:32.343 --> 00:14:34.038
| don’t have anything like that.

00:14:34.779 --> 00:14:35.871
You sure?

00:14:36.247 --> 00:14:40.877
If you insist, I’m a bit
more studious than most people.

00:14:41.052 --> 00:14:45.751
You also have the ability
to hire a stranger and go on a treasure hunt.

00:14:46.023 --> 00:14:47.320
That’s more than enough.

00:14:48.025 --> 00:14:49.617
Don’t make me laugh.

00:14:49.827 --> 00:14:53.422
How could my knowledge
be helpful in a place like this?

00:14:55.633 --> 00:14:56.793
What’s wrong?

00:15:00.171 --> 00:15:01.536
Isn't this...

00:15:05.843 --> 00:15:08.078
| found a way out.

00:15:08.079 --> 00:15:09.273
| get it!

00:15:09.447 --> 00:15:12.450
This will turn into a bamboo-leaf boat
so we can send an SOS—

00:15:12.450 --> 00:15:13.617
Wrong!

00:15:13.618 --> 00:15:16.454
This underground lake
must be connected to someplace above,

00:15:16.454 --> 00:15:18.979
and this leaf must’ve drifted from there.

00:15:19.624 --> 00:15:21.558
So if we can find where it came from...

00:15:23.594 --> 00:15:25.858
See, your knowledge came in handy.

00:15:27.899 --> 00:15:32.836
But we don’t know if the opening
is large enough for anyone to fit though...

00:15:33.204 --> 00:15:36.731
and even if it is, holding one’s breath
that long is another issue...

00:15:37.041 --> 00:15:41.671
Don’t worry. I'll keep you safe from drowning
and from frightening things.

00:15:45.349 --> 00:15:46.816
How is this possible?

00:15:47.151 --> 00:15:49.585
Your whole body is covered
with a shield of air.

00:15:50.221 --> 00:15:51.779
You can keep breathing normally.

00:15:52.256 --> 00:15:53.123
Okay.

00:15:53.124 --> 00:15:55.659
And I'll lead you by the hand.

00:15:55.660 --> 00:15:57.995
That sounds scarier than anything.

00:15:57.995 --> 00:15:59.087
So harsh.

00:15:59.363 --> 00:16:01.593
Now, here’s another magic spell for you.

00:16:06.270 --> 00:16:07.396
Seriously?

00:16:08.739 --> 00:16:10.373
Rahzel, what’s going on?

00:16:10.374 --> 00:16:11.875
You need to get ready, too.

00:16:11.876 --> 00:16:14.208
I'm fine, don’t mind me.

00:16:14.712 --> 00:16:15.974
We're going on ahead.

00:16:18.416 --> 00:16:19.383
Well...

00:16:28.893 --> 00:16:32.294
Well, | guess | should prepare myself.

00:16:35.833 --> 00:16:37.994
| can’t seem to get full control over my body...

00:16:42.006 --> 00:16:43.200
N-not good.

00:16:43.674 --> 00:16:46.404
How am | supposed to swim anyway?

00:16:49.547 --> 00:16:53.317
Tell me. If those two behind you
were drowning simultaneously,

00:16:53.317 --> 00:16:54.614
which would you choose?

00:16:56.487 --> 00:16:57.545
Oh, jeez...

00:16:58.523 --> 00:17:01.014
isn't that obvious?

00:17:20.745 --> 00:17:21.871
Here, take my hand.

00:17:22.246 --> 00:17:25.482
What? It doesn’t look any different from earlier.

00:17:25.483 --> 00:17:28.350
Well, why don’t we start exploring?

00:17:30.354 --> 00:17:32.049
What’s taking that idiot so long?

00:17:32.290 --> 00:17:35.760
Maybe she’s chasing fish like a stray cat.

00:17:35.760 --> 00:17:36.852
You know...

00:17:37.962 --> 00:17:42.626
| didn’t take her seriously before,
but is it true that she can’t swim?

00:17:50.308 --> 00:17:52.776
| had a hard time controlling my body.

00:17:53.010 --> 00:17:55.877
| freaked out and accidentally lifted the spell,
and look what happened.

00:17:56.247 --> 00:17:57.407
Rahzel...

00:17:57.548 --> 00:18:00.517
I'm not saying I'm the kind who sinks like a rock.

00:18:00.885 --> 00:18:02.785
It’s just, I'd never actually swam before.

00:18:03.354 --> 00:18:04.412
Are you out of your mind?!

00:18:04.589 --> 00:18:07.758
Why didn’t you ask for help
without being stubborn?

00:18:07.758 --> 00:18:10.560
Or did you pity me for attempting
to go beyond my ability?

00:18:10.561 --> 00:18:11.425
You’re wrong.

00:18:12.296 --> 00:18:16.062
Seeing you trying so hard
inspired me to do the same.

00:18:18.603 --> 00:18:19.637
Oh, yeah...

00:18:19.637 --> 00:18:21.366
| can answer the question you had...

00:18:21.772 --> 00:18:24.332
What if these two are drowning?

00:18:24.976 --> 00:18:26.841
| don’t like complications,
so they can both die.

00:18:27.445 --> 00:18:31.506
I mean, whichever | choose,
the other might haunt me.

00:18:31.916 --> 00:18:34.908
Besides, | wouldn’t be much of a lifesaver
when | can’t even swim.

00:18:35.386 --> 00:18:36.944
So, feel free to die, both of you.

00:18:37.388 --> 00:18:38.787
Right back at you.

00:18:44.395 --> 00:18:46.158
All right, all right.

00:18:47.164 --> 00:18:48.791
il tell you what.

00:18:49.600 --> 00:18:52.933
If you both drown, | will drown with you.

00:18:53.137 --> 00:18:58.006
So you should try hard to save me
while saving yourselves.

00:19:00.711 --> 00:19:03.612
| doubt this is the answer
you wanted to hear, though.

00:19:06.984 --> 00:19:08.212
There’s a light...

00:19:09.053 --> 00:19:10.520
| can see the light.

00:19:11.989 --> 00:19:13.183
Sunrise?

00:19:16.594 --> 00:19:17.891
| remember now.

00:19:18.362 --> 00:19:22.560
That’s what my grandfather wanted to show us,
the precious treasure.

00:19:27.705 --> 00:19:28.865
A fossil?

00:19:29.106 --> 00:19:29.868
Yeah.

00:19:30.908 --> 00:19:33.138
This is what my grandfather left for us.

00:19:34.111 --> 00:19:38.377
It’s the light to shine on my life.

00:19:39.717 --> 00:19:42.185
It’s been trapped within this ancient fossil,

00:19:42.486 --> 00:19:45.785
and yet it’s still spreading its wings
as if it’s about to fly away...

00:19:46.857 --> 00:19:51.658
by believing in its own strength
to run towards the future.

00:19:52.630 --> 00:19:55.064
Thank you... Grandfather.

00:19:57.702 --> 00:19:59.737
You sure that’s lucrative?

00:19:59.737 --> 00:20:01.637
Somewhat, | guess.

00:20:02.073 --> 00:20:04.166
By the way, | was wondering...

00:20:04.375 --> 00:20:07.811
what made you decide
to help with the treasure hunt?

00:20:08.145 --> 00:20:10.413
We had an agreement, too.

00:20:10.414 --> 00:20:12.780
With her younger sister.

00:20:14.085 --> 00:20:18.189
Do me a favor. My sister might try
going to the cave, so please...

00:20:18.189 --> 00:20:20.248
Sure, leave it to us.

00:20:21.992 --> 00:20:23.289
That figures.

00:20:28.733 --> 00:20:31.293
You sure you want to leave it as it is?

00:20:31.569 --> 00:20:35.369
Yeah, | already obtained what | need.

00:20:35.873 --> 00:20:36.999
So I’ve decided...

00:20:37.842 --> 00:20:39.310
I’m going to run away from home.

00:20:39.310 --> 00:20:40.311
Huh?

00:20:40.311 --> 00:20:42.012
Right now, right this moment.

00:20:42.012 --> 00:20:44.776
Not again. Talk about going to extremes.

00:20:45.216 --> 00:20:48.743
Once things settle down,
ll talk to my parents about college.

00:20:49.053 --> 00:20:50.816
| just have to remain determined until then.

00:20:51.589 --> 00:20:55.150
Just like that fossil, I’ll keep trying.

00:20:55.993 --> 00:21:01.761
Besides, seeing you trying so hard
inspired me to do the same.

00:21:02.166 --> 00:21:03.963
What? Are you copying me?

00:21:04.268 --> 00:21:05.565
How annoying.

00:21:07.505 --> 00:21:09.306
Are you blushing? How cute.

00:21:09.306 --> 00:21:11.900
That’s enough. I'll get going now.

00:21:12.543 --> 00:21:13.407
Bye.

00:21:14.044 --> 00:21:15.477
Oh, hold on!

00:21:16.847 --> 00:21:17.711
If...

00:21:18.616 --> 00:21:21.278
If we meet again somewhere,

00:21:21.652 --> 00:21:27.522
and if you happen to be in trouble,
| wouldn’t mind risking my life for you.

00:21:29.460 --> 00:21:31.758
| already knew that...

00:21:31.962 --> 00:21:33.486
you silly!

00:21:43.674 --> 00:21:47.344
As | hear the sound of laughter

00:21:47.344 --> 00:21:50.973
Coming from the room next door

00:21:51.148 --> 00:21:58.350
| slowly wake up to the morning that | adore

00:21:58.722 --> 00:22:05.958
Somewhere | dreamed of a painting

00:22:06.230 --> 00:22:13.534
| just painted a new chair for you

00:22:13.704 --> 00:22:18.204
Even if the sorrowful story

00:22:20.644 --> 00:22:29.348
Is lying in wait beyond the curtain

00:22:31.355 --> 00:22:38.591
Even if we may feel like strangers tomorrow

00:22:38.863 --> 00:22:45.996
| believe in the perfect miracle that you'll still be here

00:22:46.303 --> 00:22:53.641
The hand you reached out shows no sign of parting

00:22:53.978 --> 00:23:01.714
As | grow teary-eyed, | just want to hold you now
